<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hōjō Ujiyasu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1515">1515</a>–<a href="/years/1571">1571</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Hojo Ujiyasu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hōjō Ujiyasu was the third head of the Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-clan">Hōjō clan</a> and one of the leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku</a> warlords. His night attack at Kawagoe in 1546 broke a coalition of the Uesugi and made the Hōjō masters of the Kantō. He carried out land surveys and tax reforms and defended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawara">Odawara</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-kenshin">Uesugi Kenshin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hojo-ujiyasu.jpg" alt="Hōjō Ujiyasu" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ujiyasu_Hojo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
